[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=- VERSION HISTORY ----------------------------------------------
  Cmn2=--------------------\\\\v3.0  8/4/2025  Generated by AI at the instruction||1
  Cmn3=of RGW\\- Wanted to add JSON files to the mix\\    8/5/2025  Modified||1
  Cmn4=by AI at the request of RGW\\- Added File_Exists_FB feedback\\-||1
  Cmn5=Added Delete functionality\\- Added File_Busy_FB feedback\\- Added||1
  Cmn6=File_Size and integrity checks\\- Added CSV and INI formats; updated||1
  Cmn7=format order\\- Added Backup/Rollback functionality\\- Changed File_Size||1
  Cmn8=to serial output with formatted size (bytes/KB/MB)\\- Added optional||1
  Cmn9=encryption support (AES) with Encrypt enable and Encryption_Key\\
  Cmn10=- Added File_Encrypted_FB feedback to indicate if the file on disk||1
  Cmn11=is encrypted (via header detection)\\- Added Backup_Exists_FB feedback||1
  Cmn12=to indicate if the backup file exists\\    8/6/2025  Modified by||1
  Cmn13=AI at the request of RGW\\- Added optional backup history with Enable_Backup_Hist
  Cmn14=ory input\\- Added Format_Override analog input to override Format||1
  Cmn15=parameter at runtime\\- Added Filename_Override string input to||1
  Cmn16=override Filename parameter at runtime\\- Added Delete_Backup digital||1
  Cmn17=input to delete the .bak file\\- Made Format parameter and override||1
  Cmn18=1-based (1=Text to 6=Binary)\\    8/6/2025  Modified by RGW\\- Requirements||1
  Cmn19=for File_Location and FilePath_Overrifde$ have changed; the filename||1
  Cmn20=and file extension has been\\    removed\\- Removed FilePath_Override$||1
  Cmn21=serial input\\- Added Filename parameter and Filename_Override serial||1
  Cmn22=input\\- Requirements for Filename and Filename_Override have changed;||1
  Cmn23=the file extension is now omitted from the name\\- File Extensions||1
  Cmn24=are now automatically appended to the Filename and Filename_Override,||1
  Cmn25=based on the value of Format\\    and/or Format_Override\\\\v3.1||1
  Cmn26=||12/25/2026  RGW\\- Added File_Not_Exist_FB, which is actual, rather||1
  Cmn27=than derivative\\\\v3.1.1  5/1/2026  RGW\\- Corrected text detection||1
  Cmn28=in the Read() block causing signals to sometimes not be read\\-||1
  Cmn29=Removed parameter formatting from the Simpl+ code in preparation||1
  Cmn30=for packaging inside a Simpl module wrapper\\\\v3.1.2  7/16/2026||1
  Cmn31=||1RGW / AI\\- Fixed Digital_Output_[x] not asserting after a successful||1
  Cmn32=read (explicit 0/1 digital assignment from\\  Simpl# ushort values)\\
  Cmn33=- JSON read now accepts industry-standard JSON: optional crc32 (no||1
  Cmn34=hard integrity reject), case-insensitive\\  property names, optional||1
  Cmn35=data/signalData wrappers, short arrays, boolean/numeric digital||1
  Cmn36=elements\\- Paired Simpl# source: FileReader20260623.cs (rebuild||1
  Cmn37=FileReader20260623.clz after updating)\\\\v3.2.0  7/16/2026  RGW||1
  Cmn38=/ AI\\- On successful Write, copy Digital/Analog/Serial inputs to||1
  Cmn39=the corresponding outputs (explicit 0/1 for digitals)\\- Enable_Auto_Create||1
  Cmn40=when high:\\    * File missing -> Set_Default_Values -> wait Default_Settle_Time||1
  Cmn41=-> Write (then I->O copy on success)\\    * File exists -> automatic||1
  Cmn42=Read onto outputs (startup / path change restore)\\- Does not overwrite||1
  Cmn43=existing files on auto-create; one auto action per effective path||1
  Cmn44=until path changes\\- Intended to replace external Not_Exist ->||1
  Cmn45=defaults -> Write and Exist -> Read startup routines in SIMPL\\\\
  Cmn46=v3.2.1  10/13/2026  RGW / AI\\- Match_Partial finds a file whose||1
  Cmn47=name contains Filename or Filename_Override\\- Several matches use||1
  Cmn48=the first name alphabetically\\- No match keeps the exact name,||1
  Cmn49=so auto-create can write config.json\\- Filename_FB reports the||1
  Cmn50=selected file name with its extension\\- Paired Simpl# source: FileReader20261013
  Cmn51=.cs. Library FileReader_v3\\
[END]
